{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"a\">\n  <datamodel><data id=\"list\" expr=\"[{name: 'first'}]\"/></datamodel>\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <onentry>\n      <log expr=\"list.0\"/>\n      <log expr=\"list.0.name\"/>\n      <assign location=\"list.0\" expr=\"1\"/>\n    </onentry>\n    <transition event=\"go\" target=\"b\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"b\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-dot-zero-index.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":3,"warnings":3},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-dot-zero-index.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":2,"byteOffset":217,"endColumn":24,"endLine":5,"startColumn":22,"startLine":5},"insertedContent":{"text":"[0]"}}]}],"description":{"text":"index with `[0]`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-dot-zero-index.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":24,"endLine":5,"startColumn":22,"startLine":5}}}],"message":{"markdown":"ecmascript syntax error in `expr`: `.0` is not a property access\n\n**Note:** an expression that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` whenever it is evaluated\n\n**Help:** a property name cannot start with a digit; index with brackets: `[0]`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"ecmascript syntax error in `expr`: `.0` is not a property access"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":219,"start":217},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `expr`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-dot-zero-index.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":24,"endLine":5,"startColumn":18,"startLine":5}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML038"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-dot-zero-index.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":2,"byteOffset":244,"endColumn":24,"endLine":6,"startColumn":22,"startLine":6},"insertedContent":{"text":"[0]"}}]}],"description":{"text":"index with `[0]`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-dot-zero-index.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":24,"endLine":6,"startColumn":22,"startLine":6}}}],"message":{"markdown":"ecmascript syntax error in `expr`: `.0` is not a property access\n\n**Note:** an expression that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` whenever it is evaluated\n\n**Help:** a property name cannot start with a digit; index with brackets: `[0]`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"ecmascript syntax error in `expr`: `.0` is not a property access"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":246,"start":244},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `expr`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-dot-zero-index.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":29,"endLine":6,"startColumn":18,"startLine":6}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML038"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-dot-zero-index.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":2,"byteOffset":283,"endColumn":31,"endLine":7,"startColumn":29,"startLine":7},"insertedContent":{"text":"[0]"}}]}],"description":{"text":"index with `[0]`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-dot-zero-index.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":31,"endLine":7,"startColumn":29,"startLine":7}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`location` is not an assignable ecmascript location: `.0` is not a property access\n\n**Note:** a location expression must name a place in the data model that can be assigned, such as a variable name or a property access like `a.b` or `a[0]`\n\n**Help:** a property name cannot start with a digit; index with brackets: `[0]`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9.2 Location Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`location` is not an assignable ecmascript location: `.0` is not a property access"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":285,"start":283},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `location`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-dot-zero-index.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":31,"endLine":7,"startColumn":25,"startLine":7}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML039"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML 1.0 §5.9.4: \"The SCXML Processor MAY reject documents containing syntactically ill-formed expressions at document load time, or it MAY wait and place 'error.execution' in the internal event queue at runtime when the expressions are evaluated.\" This toolchain takes the second option, so the document compiles and the expression raises `error.execution` whenever it is evaluated (a condition is then false and the rest of an executable-content block is skipped); this check runs only when the host supplies the data model's parse-only syntax capability (the native CLI links the ECMAScript and XPath checkers). Each finding names the offending source text and, where a repair is certain to parse, offers it: ECMAScript habits in XPath (`==` to `=`, `&&` to `and`, `||` to `or`, `!x` to `not(x)`, `length()` to `string-length()`), a stray `=` in ECMAScript (`x === = 3`), word operators, quoting, and more. The XPath data model has no script language, so a non-empty `<script>` is reported too"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: apply the suggested repair, or fix the syntax at the marked position following the finding's help; for XPath, use XPath 1.0 operators and functions (`=`, `and`, `or`, `not()`, `string-length()`, `count()`).\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML038` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#ecma-profile","id":"SCXML038","name":"SCXML038","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an expression or script does not parse in the selected data model"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"`location`, `idlocation`, `namelist` items, and `<foreach item/index>` must name an assignable place; SCXML 1.0 defines the run-time outcome of one that does not, so the document compiles: §5.9.2 \"If a location expression cannot be evaluated to yield a valid location, the SCXML processor MUST place the error 'error.execution' in the internal event queue\", and §4.6 \"if 'item' does not specify a legal variable name, the SCXML processor MUST terminate execution of the <foreach> element and the block that contains it, and place the error error.execution on the internal event queue\". In ECMAScript an assignable place is a variable or a property access such as `data.field` or `data[0]`; in XPath it is an expression that selects existing nodes, such as `$data` or `$data/field` (`a.b` is one variable name containing a dot, and `a[0]` is a predicate)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: ECMAScript: use a variable name or a member expression such as `data.field`; XPath: use a `$`-rooted path to a declared variable such as `$data/field`.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §5.9.2 Location Expressions\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML039` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#LocationExpressions","id":"SCXML039","name":"SCXML039","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a location is not assignable in the selected data model"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}